Charlie schrieb:
> For example, I have a Samurai skilled in long sword and basic in
> dagger.
> Should I hone up either of those skills before going developing two
> weaponing? And why?

The minimum skill of each weapon and of your two-weapon proficiency
is effective. So enhance both, your weapon skills and two-weaponing
skill; first enhance the individual weapon's proficiency exercising
single-weapon combat, then exercise your two-weaponing proficiency.
If your character can only get Basic in any of the skills it's an
inferior weapon choice; pick those (class appropriate) weapons whose
proficiencies you can maximize. It's also a waste to advance skill
slots to Expert[*] if you intend two-weaponing but can't get beyond
Skilled with either of the used weapons.

[*] Of course it still makes sense to get, say, daggers to Expert
even if you can only to Skilled with two-weaponing, because your
daggers skill will also be very useful when using them as missiles.

